{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548737-mithras-and-the-secret-reasons-behind-his-move-to-britannia","id":1548737,"title":"Mithras and the secret reasons behind his move to Britannia","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-02-23T13:33:32-08:00","id":1548737,"title":"Mithras and the secret reasons behind his move to Britannia","content":"Please don't take <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QjzTYdd8jPY\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> too seriously.<br /> <br /> (Though he <i><b>was</b></i> persian....) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-23-2025, 08:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-23T20:39:36-08:00","id":1548745,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I always questioned that.<br /> <br /> For me, he wanted a real far off place, with close to no vampire, and not much dense population. So he moved to an island full of &quot;brittunculi&quot; according to the Romans, to contemplate things in deep thought while still having a domain with blood. Far from the big centers of Cainite action at the time.<br /> Maybe there he desired to build a Cainite society styled after his own style and wants.<br /> <br /> I also think from time to time he goes on a tour of sorts, like a warrior poet of old, visiting places of his cult, or even going as far as his homeland. Although travel is super dangerous, he is a methuseleah of much skill, and has a network of loyal cults.<br /> Since just making him an arrogant selfish prick makes the legend of Mithras a bit too samey as all other oldies, I prefered to imagine him as the more &quot;honor your words&quot; &quot;break no oaths&quot; kind of religious Mithras that we got in history. Something like a king of judges, in a time where the were no sects to enforce favors being paid. Which would also put Mithras close to the Banu Haqim, doubling both as a reason to have Haqim himself visit Mithras, and a nice irony that he would end up possessing a Haquimite. <br /> <br /> So yeah, maybe he knew Britain would become an empire, or maybe he just thought it was a nice island with human herd and peace and quiet for him to use it as resort and hermitage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-24T06:42:53-08:00","id":1548752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548737-mithras-and-the-secret-reasons-behind-his-move-to-britannia?p=1548745#post1548745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I always questioned that.<br /> <br /> For me, he wanted a real far off place, with close to no vampire, and not much dense population. So he moved to an island full of &quot;brittunculi&quot; according to the Romans, to contemplate things in deep thought while still having a domain with blood. Far from the big centers of Cainite action at the time.<br /> Maybe there he desired to build a Cainite society styled after his own style and wants.<br /> <br /> I also think from time to time he goes on a tour of sorts, like a warrior poet of old, visiting places of his cult, or even going as far as his homeland. Although travel is super dangerous, he is a methuseleah of much skill, and has a network of loyal cults.<br /> Since just making him an arrogant selfish prick makes the legend of Mithras a bit too samey as all other oldies, I prefered to imagine him as the more &quot;honor your words&quot; &quot;break no oaths&quot; kind of religious Mithras that we got in history. Something like a king of judges, in a time where the were no sects to enforce favors being paid. Which would also put Mithras close to the Banu Haqim, doubling both as a reason to have Haqim himself visit Mithras, and a nice irony that he would end up possessing a Haquimite.<br /> <br /> So yeah, maybe he knew Britain would become an empire, or maybe he just thought it was a nice island with human herd and peace and quiet for him to use it as resort and hermitage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have my doubts on this one.<br /> <br /> There were already two 4th generation Ventrue there before him. Tiamat being one of them and then Julian Cerialis sire. Perhaps Mithras saw an opportunity there.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-24T13:42:12-08:00","id":1548757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548737-mithras-and-the-secret-reasons-behind-his-move-to-britannia?p=1548752#post1548752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have my doubts on this one.<br /> <br /> There were already two 4th generation Ventrue there before him. Tiamat being one of them and then Julian Cerialis sire. Perhaps Mithras saw an opportunity there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reasonably sure Tiamat only comes to the Isles after the sack of Rome, so about 1-2 centuries <b>after </b>Mithras own move, depending on <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sack_of_Rome#Historical_events\" target=\"_blank\">which one</a> her tale mean.<br /> <br /> Julian Cerialis' sire.... well, like everything related to the generation and lineage of DA characters, i'd say take the book info with a grain of salt. Even without considering how fragile, not to say pitifully weak many of these characters can seem to be for their supposed ages and generations, the fact this mysterious unnamed ancient Ventrue is destroyed by his childe in a timeframe very close to <i>another </i>ancient Ventrue deciding to move into the Britain is awfully convenient, not to say suspicious.<br /> <br /> What if the deposed Prince of Eboracum WAS Mithras, who edited the memory of his childe and supporters about the actual events for convoluted reasons of his own, for example?<br /> And that without even going into the possibility of Cerialis' 5th gen blood coming from successful diablerie instead of pure lineage. Lots of room for twists and complications.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-25T00:28:53-08:00","id":1548760,"title":"","content":"If you don't mind I would liek to share my quasi-headcanon supported by lore in this matter<br /> <br /> Artemis Orthia is believed the Antediluvian's first Children... or at least the first who survived<br /> Artemis Orthia's Embrace is usually placed around 5000 BC, after shortly or in the Second City. Since there is at least a 3000 years gap between the First and the Second City and there was a Deluge exactly because the Vampires broke Caine's rule (among others...) to no to Sire I found that higly unlikely Veddartha not Embraced before Artemis Orthia<br /> Things here get a little bit complicated since in theory the Ventrue Antediluvian died outside of the gates of the City - usually Troile is credited for the kill, but Lasombra and Set (not necesarily the same person as Sutekh...) or even one of his own Children are candidates.<br /> So right there we end up a funny little problem: for a dead Antediluvian he was quite active and &quot;fertile&quot; and spawne many children including possible his &quot;first&quot; Artemis Orthia<br /> Since then, the clan has had a dissociated relationship with their Antediluvian founder. Sometimes the Ventrue claim to be the only clan free of an Antediluvian ancestor's manipulations, sometimes outright denying that the Antediluvians ever existed, and other times claiming authority over their Kindred through their esteemed progenitor's lineage.<br /> The Ventrue requires a Child to know their lineage up to the &quot;dead&quot; founder who have no power over them or not even existed... but you have to know regardless, and just ignore the fact usually he Embraced your great ancestor after he died<br /> In my personal oppinion this is the classic case of a Dominate at work on par with whats happened during the Lasombra Antediluvian's &quot;death&quot;...<br /> Anyhow, move on<br /> I don't think the Second city was that far from the First<br /> Here let me take a little detour<br /> Where was the First City? Easy enough, it was in the Land of Nod<br /> 'kay<br /> Where was the Land of Nod?<br /> We know that one too!<br /> The Land of Nod was located east of Eden where Caine was exiled by God after the murder of his brother Abel.<br /> Eden...<br /> Okay, just find the Garden of Eden...<br /> <br /> \u201cA river watering the garden flowed from Eden; from there it was separated into four headwaters. The name of the first is the Pishon; it winds through the entire land of Havilah, where there is gold. (The gold of that land is good; aromatic resin and onyx are also there.) The name of the second river is the Gihon; it winds through the entire land of Cush. The name of the third river is the Tigris; it runs along the east side of Ashur. And the fourth river is the Euphrates.\u201d<br /> <br /> Two of these rivers, the Tigris and Euphrates, still flow today. The Pishon and the Gihon dried up soon after the close of the last ice age. All four rivers flow or flowed into the Persian Gulf. They come close together in the southeastern part of today\u2019s Persian Gulf. Presently, this location is about 200 feet below sea level. During most of the last ice age, it was above sea level.<br /> There are many speculations about where the land of Nod may be, but it is safe to say, the Land of Nod was somewhere the area of today's Afghanistan and Pakistan - the area's geography would suit the WoD description, not to mention the First City, Enoch there in the Toreador interpretation was called Ubar, meaning &quot;Queen of Frankincense.&quot;<br /> Frankincense is an aromatic resin from the Boswellia sacra tree, and from India, and the Middle East, frankincense oil has been important both socially and economically as an ingredient in incense and perfumes for thousands of years<br /> Not to mention would make all those Antediluvan travels to the East much more realistic, and would explain why there is a strong Cainite presence in India to the point the Danava believe themselves to be the guardians of their Antediluvian (pitri, or &quot;father&quot;), whom they call Veddhartha. These Danava claim that the Ventrue are in fact an errant antitribu bloodline of the Danava. The Salubri say that Saulot achieved a transcendent spiritual state in the Indian city of Golconda, which falls within territory controlled by the Danava - some even believe that the very notion of Golconda originated from the Danava<br /> Now this little sidetrack, let me explain my theory, built on these!<br /> Saulot and Set said to be brothers (and with the triplets Malkav, Malakai, and Arikel and their sister Nathema,)<br /> Saulot demonstreated a very strong dual personality, Zao-Lat and Saulot, the White Worm and the the Prophet, Hun and his P'o separated - the Salubri even have a quesy-canon option to transform their beast to an awakened P'o and start their Dharmic journy<br /> Why? Because the Land of Nod basically was the part of the Middle Kingdom or at least was on the border to be effected by the &quot;laws of the Middle Kingdom and the Yama Kings&quot;<br /> Maybe his brother Set/Sutekh is similar - and to be fair, Malkav, Malakai, and Arikel and their sister Nathema not that &quot;sane&quot; either, one even became a Demon (ascended to a Yama Queen perhaps?)<br /> Set and Typhon , a &quot;good&quot; (or at leats not THAT bad) and a bad side - witch is witch is up for interpretation<br /> Set story how he returned from the udnerword is very similar of the Kuei-jin creation how someone return from Yomi<br /> Maybe Set and Saulot walked the same path with the same results - and this is mirrored in their Clan.The Witches and Warriors were replaced just like the Salubri and consantly evolved depending on what personality the rational Hun or the demonci P'o was dominant, just in Set case he stayed in one body<br /> <br /> Sorry, it will make sense soon, I promise<br /> Haqim had a little quarel with Caine back in the days (I will not ellborate this, I promise) and his followers carried his body to the nearby mountains where he made his home Alamut<br /> Today we know Alamut, also known as Alah Amut (literally &quot;Eagle's Nest&quot;), the headquarters of the Assamite clan located somewhere in Afghanistan<br /> And from there Haqim for a while - during the Baali Wars - returned to the Second City and Saulot &quot;tricked&quot; him to become the Judge - so they say - but all and all, he never really trusted Saulot. Eventually he moved back &quot;home&quot;<br /> So we now have a pretty good idea where the Second City was probably and we can start to map the Journeys of Veddhartha.<br /> <br /> So the Ancient travelled, like his Childe and we have the first two kids<br /> Artemis Orthia and her broodmate Medon - but let us stop here for a moment - remember what I said about the whole he may had children before Artemis? <br /> They were probably Embraced around the Second City, but thanks to the whole Danava thing I would say Veddartha the Antediluvian Embraces Veddartha, the Younger in India around this time too possibly his true first childe and have a foothold in that area (and if you are familiar with the Secret Masters and how the Antediluvian turned his palace in to a fortress and started hoarding artefacts it would make sense), another oddball is Nefer-meri-Isis, she was a fierce girl, Tales within the clan tell that she single-handedly fought Set and managed to incapacitate him and she never held a throne, instead preferring to wander the African continent. A little lore tidbit is Osiris' sire Typhon who was usually believed to be Lasombra or Brujah Antediluvian and both had quite a history with the Antediluvian. It actually make sense when he Embraced there and moved a piece on the board one of them did the same just with Osiris. Sutekh was cought in the middle - I am convinced Set and Sutekh are not the same person. Eventually I will write something about that theory of mine) )<br /> Back to Artemis and Medon; they either travelled with her Sire (untill &quot; a great betrayal ripped the one known as Artemis Orthia apart from her sire.&quot;) or alone but eventually she settled in the Peloponnes.<br /> Medon, untill his death was called &quot;God-King of the Aegean&quot; and ruled an island openly as God and treated his subject so poorly the mortals rebelled and destroyed him around 200 BC forcing his Clan to rethink they unlife (a little funny trivia, Medon - among many - was the name of a Centaur at the wedding of Pirithous and Hippodamia. Centauromachy, the Lapiths battle was with the Centaurs at the wedding feast of Pirithous. The Centaurs had been invited, but, unused to wine, their wild nature came to the fore... red liquid and sudden frenzy? Now where did I heard that one before?)<br /> Now since they were broodmates but porbably not sired there it is safe to assume they accompanied their Sire to that area or traveled alone - but given the geography it is higly likely the Antediluvian passed there eventually<br /> It make sense, since the next in line is Arakur of Ur in ancient Sumer who been Embraced around 3000 BC (or 2000 BC - His Child, Lantla was Embraced before 3000 BC, but Arakur already lived in Ziggurat of Ur at that time, which was built in approximately 2000 BC so either a typo or he spent millenium building that thing... actually both could work)<br /> So the Travels so far:<br /> Second City - India and Egypt - Summer<br /> Move along in the timeline, is 1258 BC, the Embrace of Mithras - many claims he is not the direct Child but actually there is a lot of support Veddartha was the Antediluvian and Veddartha, the Younger in India were Sire and Child but since this essay starts to become bloated, I will not list why Mithras is not a diablerist and why a true Child)<br /> Second City - India and Egypt- Summer- Persia - then the dates of Sparta strats to add up, so he probably arrived with or without Artemis and Medon to Greece - and io and behold!<br /> Circa 700 BE the Antedilivan Embraces Alexander in Ancient Greece.<br /> Tidy isn't it?<br /> He then moved again westward and embraced Tinia before 480 BC (her embrace is not rellay known, but the Julia Antasia, her Child was Embraced 480 BC so it had to be before that) in Etruria (Itally) who would come to rule over the Etruscans.<br /> and before 600 BC he Embraced Antonius the Gaul, originally known as Antiorix (which mean 'Last King') and Erik Eigermann (According to the book France by Night, Erik Eigermann's original name was Ueruic, which means &quot;Great fighter&quot;), and when Massalia was founded they arrived to take control of most the Ancient Gaul<br /> So the Travels so far:<br /> Second City - India and Egypt - Summer - Persia - Ancient Greece - Etruria/Ancient Itally - Ancient Gaul<br /> <br /> At this point no more know kids, but we are ate the moment in Ancient Gaul, France and what is next...?<br /> Yes, the British Isles<br /> The mysterious Prince of Eboracum died around 306 CE<br /> So between Antonius the Gaul (who was embraced around 600 BC) and Prince of Eboracum's death in 306 CE a thousand year or so passed, even if he was Embraced right after the few years of Antonius' Embrace, the Prince was not THAT old and Ventrue older than him fall victim to the fangs of others - like Antonius for example<br /> To me, given the Journeys of Veddhartha?<br /> It actually make sense and logical to the Ancient to end up in the British Isles, Mithras interest in the place and later why the Britihs Empire was so keen to claim India - the Antediluvian after the Embrace of the Prince of Eboracum went home to his last/first bastion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-25T11:16:03-08:00","id":1548765,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the original reason being something to do with the fact that Roman Britannia had a garrison three legions (and associated supporting elements) strong, which would certainly appeal to Mithras\u2019 soldierly inclinations: that it would also allow him to put a moat (What we now call the English Channel, at least north of <i>la Manche</i>) between himself and the most powerful concentration of vampires in Europe could be a secondary motivation.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, he might well have appreciated the ability to slip over the line between Rome and not-Rome at discretion (Though that would also be the case in Germany, so it\u2019s intriguing to wonder why he didn\u2019t set up there).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-25T20:50:01-08:00","id":1548778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548737-mithras-and-the-secret-reasons-behind-his-move-to-britannia?p=1548765#post1548765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I wonder if the original reason being something to do with the fact that Roman Britannia had a garrison three legions (and associated supporting elements) strong, which would certainly appeal to Mithras\u2019 soldierly inclinations: that it would also allow him to put a moat (What we now call the English Channel, at least north of <i>la Manche</i>) between himself and the most powerful concentration of vampires in Europe could be a secondary motivation.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, he might well have appreciated the ability to slip over the line between Rome and not-Rome at discretion (Though that would also be the case in Germany, so it\u2019s intriguing to wonder why he didn\u2019t set up there).</div> </div> </div> </div>An advantage with Britain might have been that there was, I would think, more urban and Roman comforts in Britain than in Germania along with more distance to other powerful Cainites?<br /> <br /> I don't know for sure but I would think that there would've been some pretty old Gangrel hanging out beyond the Rhine and Mithras might have considered it more cost effective to take over Roman Albion rather than carve out his domain among the Gangrel and tribesmen of Germania and then carefully cultivate urbanization and such among the Germans while keeping the neighbors off his lawn before he would get to work with what he could almost instantly get in Roman Britain.<br /> <br /> I could be wrong of course as the Germanic peoples were not exactly in stasis during the Roman Empire's lifespan in our world.<br /> <br /> A question I would put to the thread is this: Roman Britain was a source of repeated usurpers and even an attempt to break away during the Late Roman Empire. Was this just the kine doing their thing or did Mithras have a hand in this, and if so, what was his agenda with that?<br /> <br /> EDITED: Forgive me if I got some stuff regarding the VtM timeline wrong. I am no scholar of VtM lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-27T06:47:48-08:00","id":1548803,"title":"","content":"I suspect that Mithras would be happy so long as there were military men to subsist upon, battles to be commanded and rivals kept firmly in their place (Whether in submission or the grave).<br /> <br /> Well, right up until he got bored with being a God-king and decided to take one of his sabbaticals (I tend to run with the idea that Mithras loves being worshipped, but gets painfully bored with his cultists from time-to-time: some part of him is always much happier with soldierly camaraderie and generalship, but his raw personal power and love of dominion obliges him to operate on a level far above most of his Kindred, never mind mere mortals*).<br /> <br /> <br /> *I\u2019ve come to suspect that LONDON BY NIGHT would be much more coherent if it were rewritten with an eye to putting PCs in a role comparable to Thomas Cromwell in WOLF HALL - if one can keep in with the local Prince one can achieve anything, but the Prince could do ANYTHING and at short notice too (Which is why so many potential Power Players lie low or outright flee while the Elephant is in the castle).<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a bit of this implicit in the book\u2019s set-up, but it doesn\u2019t seem to be very well-expressed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-02T11:02:09-08:00","id":1548881,"title":"","content":"I go with that Mithras wanted to create his own fiefdom and heard of the many challenges that the frontier would give him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-03T11:17:44-08:00","id":1548912,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm now convinced that it's because he wanted to wear pants again. That video can't be argued with.<br /> <br /> OOC, I'm fairly certain they put Mithras in London because of the very famous Mithraeum discovered in London in 1954. Everything else is just contrived to get him there.<br /> <br /> Now IC, the most obvious reason to me why a powerful elder vampire would want to move to a relative backwater like the British Isles (in Classical times) is that it's a self imposed exile. He wants to get away from places that have lots of powerful, aged vampires like him so he is the only one. Why? Probably not cowardice, but he might have thought it was the safest bet. He might have become involved with some kind of feud or dispute and thought it wasn't worth it.<br /> <br /> Still some kind of premonition could have been a factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-04T04:01:52-08:00","id":1548944,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s also possible that he could more easily guarantee that he was the oldest and most potent vampire in a relative backwater, making it far easier to pass himself off as a deity to his cult of admirers (That this would also put him a long, long way from the locations likeliest to preserve some traditions of him as a mere vampire - possibly even some record of past defeats and how they were contrived - might also have played some role in Mithras\u2019 decision).<br /> <br /> Also, while putting \u2018Mithras\u2019 in London might have been prompted by nothing more than the discovery &amp; presence of the Mithraeum, making the Prince of London (One of the most puissant vampires in Western Europe) a Kindred who looks like an Indian demigod, wields godlike power and stands at the head of an Ancient Roman cult just WORKS on a Gothic-Punk level (In that it absolutely sounds like something out of a Hammer Horror, but becomes quite subversive when one becomes convinced that Mithras kept thinking of Britain as <i>his</i> colony even in the days when the sun never set on the British Empire*).<br /> <br /> <br /> *Of all the disappointments associated with LONDON BY NIGHT, the greatest must be it\u2019s peculiar failure to start with -<br /> <br /> \u201cThe reason the sun never sets on the British Empire is that even God couldn\u2019t trust an Englishman in the dark.\u201d<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-04T10:56:57-08:00","id":1548958,"title":"","content":"That is the most likely reason for why Mithras went to England Atticus Cleanclaw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-04T11:20:42-08:00","id":1548961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548737-mithras-and-the-secret-reasons-behind-his-move-to-britannia?p=1548912#post1548912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Still some kind of premonition could have been a factor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have this funny headcanon Mithras got involved first the War of Silver and Iron between the Fae and the Garou then later was instrumental to spread the Wyrm/Weaver influence and the fall of the White Howlers <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-05T16:36:55-08:00","id":1548996,"title":"","content":"I have to agree that the placing of Mithras in Britain really does work best on a Doyalist level where you get all sorts of juicy stuff to play with ranging from: the literal mithraeum, the association of the later British Empire with the Roman Empire (interesting because this association was invoked both as a positive and as a negative irl), the occult concept (descended from Theosophy iirc) that Britain contained one of the central nodes of occult energy on the planet (Kenneth Anger, a student of Crowley, identifies Glastonbury as the site of the earth\u2019s pancreatic gland chakra center), etc.<br /> <br /> Britain is of course interesting in general as a lot of ideas and lore about it of course remain high in the consciousness of anglophone societies, inevitably producing a tendency towards its importance. You\u2019ve got the ancient and on-going fascination of writers with the Druids and Britain as one of the centers of the breakaway empires of the Crisis of the Third Century. You\u2019ve got the Romano-Britains before one of the true collapses of the world of antiquity in Western Europe. This leads me to then wonder if in the WoD we should maybe play around a bit with some esoteric britain topics such as, say King Arthur having some sort of syncretism with a Roman cult figure such as Mithras could provide. I think it would be funny and within WW\u2019s tradition to imply that Mithras may have been one aspect of the King Arthur legend.<br /> <br /> Then in the Middle Ages you get to play around with stuff like the legends about the Holy Grail being in Glastonbury or that the Knights Templar (after gaining knowledge in the mystery schools of the east) fled to Scotland to avoid their persecution under King Phillip the Fair (which, of course, is why Freemasonry later emerged from Scotland in 1717). I\u2019ve always thought that having the Ventrue be fascinated by freemasonry would be a perfect fit for them and it even works with their 1e/2e anxiety over the influence of \u2018secret masters\u2019.<br /> <br /> Sinister and occult Britain works even better once you get to the Victorian Era and you can imply that somehow Mithras\u2019 influence is directly connected with the expansion of the empire\u2019s power. One can really go crazy with this. One can loot Alan Moore\u2019s From Hell for inspiration on the arcane cruelty of the Occult British Empire or go back and look at Blavatsky &amp; Bulwer-Lytton for inspiration (Blavatsky is fascinating here because of how her interest in Tibet and south eastern mysticism aligns with the British expansion into India and the rumors that Blavatsky may have somehow been involved in intelligence activities wrt the Great Game &amp; Bulwer-Lytton, a man of some influence within the empire, whose dabbling in writing orientalist literature gives us the idea of a British ruling class secretly participating in a Cult of Isis, etc.)<br /> <br /> From a Doyalist perspective, Mithras\u2019 exoticism makes a lot of sense in retrospect, if we ground it by associating it with the flourishing Orientalism of the British empire at its height, with the character of Mithras as both a symbol of imperial vitality via his Roman connections and a symbol of a mysterious eastern religion synergyzing with the empire\u2019s fascination with and intervention in Asia. Mithras\u2019 proximity to power also works well as a parallel to anxieties over the empire\u2019s condition dating back to the imperial era, with the reoccurring fear that somehow the east was going to \u2018infect\u2019 the empire through contact (see stories ranging from Dracula to Fu Manchu) taken to its logical extreme: that there is no purely \u2018British\u2019 empire to infect; the outside (Asia) has been on the inside (Britain, by extension, Europe) from the very beginning.<br /> <br /> Cue the Lovecraftian break in the protagonist\u2019s psyche as they realize to their horror that their entire notion of themselves has been a lie from the beginning and that they themselves are one of the very things which they had always defined themselves against.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11637,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","user":"Gryffon15","date":". 03-05-2025, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-06T14:45:20-08:00","id":1549024,"title":"","content":"A most excellent summation, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11637_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11637\" data-vbnamecard=\"11637\">Gryffon15</a> - though it\u2019s interesting to note that Mithras was actually absent from London between AD 1798 and 1885 (When the Empire was reaching it\u2019s apogee).<br /> <br /> I wonder if he was seeing what old rivals and upstarts would try to fill the gap in his absence or just fancied a bit of \u2018War Tourism\u2019 with the Revolutionary &amp; Napoleonic Wars a-raging?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28339,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","user":"Atticus Cleanclaw","date":".  Filling in the gaps 03-06-2025, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-06T15:30:28-08:00","id":1549030,"title":"","content":"I could see Mithras wanting to travel and see old haunts from his younger nights and some sense of nostalgia and reigniting some passions again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-07T05:19:36-08:00","id":1549047,"title":"","content":"For some reason it occurred to me that while Mithras loves being a god, he can get terribly bored with being worshipped (Being, at heart, a soldierly autocrat and somewhat no-nonsense).<br /> <br /> Or perhaps he just got tired of the British weather and desired a spell in some more consistent climate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}